rt of close on on the actions and  the fourth and final theme is in some  ways the easiest to describe but the  hardest to do  so once you've got your great leadership  once you've got your perfect team once  they're doing a modern design process  the final piece to break here is around  fixing the silos between physical  digital  and service design there are so many  companies now who still have a separate  physical design  arm a separate digital arm and it really  gets in the way  of modern seamless experience that  customers have become to  expect um you know if i think of some of  the examples that stick with me  there was an example of a med tech  company  who was making products for people with  chronic disease  the way they used to think about that is  well we're a physical product company  so we need to think about viscosity we  need to think about the volume to be  injected into the body  of this particular medicine and what  they did is say that that's a very  old-fashioned way of thinking about our  industry  let's instead for a moment think about  the combination  of digital physical and service in the  form of doctors and nurses  and they started talking instead of  about a physical injection device  they started talking about reminders  that you're sick  and in fact in this particular disease  many people had about 27 reminders  uh in a given month that they were a  sick individual that they were living  under the burden of this disease  and what the company did is they said no  well let's work together to reduce that  burden  they got it from 27 reminders down to  seven  uh nine reminders sorry that you were  sick and that's when you started to have  improved patient quality of life that's  when you started to have  improved medical outcomes and that was  brilliant the fact that this company  moved from thinking about product  thinking about product and  apps and in-person services i think that  the recognition that user experience is  critical is actually becoming more  commonplace i i do believe that  we're actually seeing more companies  focus on a kind of holistic user  experience journey  and more than just optimizing as kind of  single touch point  for me one one example close to heart is  our local airport changi airport  as an example they've actually we've  talked to the team and they actually  conduct meticulous research to actually  stitch the traveler's journey  together to ultimately create a seamless  and delightful way of balancing  they call kind of hospitality and a  transportation efficiency  and i think one large thing one large  innovation they did a lot of the last  few years was to build this  uh huge kind of uh centerpiece called  jewel  to be able to complete the kind of  airport experience to wild visitors  so i totally agree with you no i'm  with you all i and i hope to be able to  uh to see jewel  uh soon and be with you mark in  singapore when you and i last went it  was a few months from completion and i'm  i'm sad that the world has changed so  much but i haven't been back since but  uh hopefully 2021 will be the uh  will be the year um i'm really excited  about what follows in today's  conversation i think that  the themes that we've touched on whether  it be the things like that breakdown of  physical and digital service like you  you're mentioning at the airport  whether it be the leadership piece  whether it be the people piece  whether it be the process piece i think  all of these sort of common sense i  think these are all things that  companies in singapore can do  i think for me it feels a little bit  like diet and exercise we all know we're  supposed to be doing it but none of us  do it  and i what i hope is today comes  something of a  a catalyst moment where many companies  can say actually no we can do these four  together  and i think we'll see a real difference  in the in the months and years that  follow in terms of performance  thanks for reminding me i do need to die  on an exercise in 2021  but these are certainly exciting results  it gives us  personally a kind of clearer picture  about how we at design singapore can  actually help further support companies  to grow to the next level
 

